  "verbalization": "Drostanolone is linked to Ar through a series of molecular relationships that converge on the 17Beta-Hydroxy Steroid pathway. The evidence suggests that Drostanolone, through its resemblance to Stanozolol and Oxandrolone, ultimately binds to Ar. This is supported by the shared lowest common ancestors among these compounds, which all point to 17Beta-Hydroxy Steroid as a central node. The similarity in molecular structure between Drostanolone and other androgens, such as Stanozolol and Oxandrolone, implies a potential for similar pharmacological effects, including the binding to Ar. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Ar through different but related compounds reinforces the likelihood of a direct or indirect interaction between Drostanolone and Ar. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of the 17Beta-Hydroxy Steroid pathway in mediating the effects of androgenic compounds, suggesting that Drostanolone may act through a similar mechanism as other androgens, potentially influencing Ar's function.",
